# PART 1 — Install Ansible

# Step 1: Update System

```bash id="d1"
sudo dnf update -y
```

## Description

* `dnf` → package manager
* `update` → updates installed packages
* `-y` → auto yes

Why important?

* Prevent dependency issues
* Ensure latest repositories

---

# Step 2: Install Ansible Core

```bash id="d2"
sudo dnf install ansible-core -y
```

## Description

Installs:

* ansible command
* ansible-playbook
* ansible-galaxy
* modules

---

# Step 3: Verify Installation

```bash id="d3"
ansible --version
```

## Example Output

```bash id="d4"
ansible [core 2.15]
```

## Important Details

Shows:

* version
* python version
* config path
* module paths

RHCE exam:
You may need to verify installation before automation tasks.

---

# PART 2 — Configure SSH

Ansible uses SSH to connect managed nodes.

---

# Step 4: Generate SSH Key

```bash id="d5"
ssh-keygen
```

## Description

Creates:

* public key
* private key

Files created:

```bash id="d6"
~/.ssh/id_rsa
~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub
```

---

# Step 5: Copy SSH Key

```bash id="d7"
ssh-copy-id student@node1
```

## Description

Copies public key to:

```bash id="d8"
~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```

on target machine.

Now passwordless login works.

---

# Step 6: Test SSH

```bash id="d9"
ssh student@node1
```

## Purpose

Verify:

* network connectivity
* authentication
* hostname resolution

---

# PART 3 — Inventory

Inventory defines managed hosts.

---

# Step 7: Create Inventory File

```bash id="d10"
mkdir inventory
vi inventory/hosts
```

Example:

```ini id="d11"
[web]
node1

[db]
node2
```

---

# Step 8: Understand Inventory Structure

## Group

```ini id="d12"
[web]
```

means:

* web = group name

---

## Hosts

```ini id="d13"
node1
node2
```

means:
managed servers.

---

# Step 9: Test Inventory

```bash id="d14"
ansible all -i inventory/hosts -m ping
```

## Command Breakdown

| Part    | Meaning        |
| ------- | -------------- |
| ansible | main command   |
| all     | all hosts      |
| -i      | inventory file |
| -m      | module         |
| ping    | test module    |

---

# Step 10: Expected Output

```bash id="d15"
node1 | SUCCESS => {
    "ping": "pong"
}
```

## Meaning

* SSH works
* Python exists
* Host reachable

---

# PART 4 — Ad-Hoc Commands

Used for quick automation.

---

# Step 11: Run Linux Command

```bash id="d16"
ansible all -a "uptime"
```

## Description

`-a`
means:
argument/command.

Executes:

```bash id="d17"
uptime
```

on all servers.

---

# Step 12: Check Disk Space

```bash id="d18"
ansible all -a "df -h"
```

## Description

Shows:

* mounted filesystems
* disk usage
* available storage

---

# Step 13: Check Memory

```bash id="d19"
ansible all -a "free -m"
```

## Description

Displays:

* RAM
* swap
* memory usage

---

# Step 14: Install Package

```bash id="d20"
ansible all -m dnf -a "name=httpd state=present" --become
```

## Breakdown

| Part          | Meaning         |
| ------------- | --------------- |
| dnf           | package module  |
| name=httpd    | package         |
| state=present | install package |
| --become      | sudo/root       |

---

# Step 15: Start Service

```bash id="d21"
ansible all -m service -a "name=httpd state=started enabled=yes"
```

## Description

| Parameter     | Meaning       |
| ------------- | ------------- |
| name          | service name  |
| state=started | start service |
| enabled=yes   | start at boot |

---

# Step 16: Create File

```bash id="d22"
ansible all -m file -a "path=/tmp/test state=touch"
```

## Description

Creates empty file:

```bash id="d23"
/tmp/test
```

---

# Step 17: Create Directory

```bash id="d24"
ansible all -m file -a "path=/opt/demo state=directory"
```

## Description

Creates directory remotely.

---

# Step 18: Copy File

```bash id="d25"
ansible all -m copy -a "src=test.txt dest=/tmp/test.txt"
```

## Description

Copies:

* local file
  → remote server

---

# Step 19: Remove File

```bash id="d26"
ansible all -m file -a "path=/tmp/test.txt state=absent"
```

## Description

Deletes:

* file
* directory

---

# PART 5 — Playbooks

Playbooks automate multiple tasks.

---

# Step 20: Create Playbook

```bash id="d27"
mkdir playbooks
vi playbooks/apache.yml
```

---

# Step 21: Write Playbook

```yaml id="d28"
---
- name: Install Apache
  hosts: web
  become: yes

  tasks:

    - name: Install package
      dnf:
        name: httpd
        state: present

    - name: Start service
      service:
        name: httpd
        state: started
        enabled: yes
```

---

# Step 22: Understand YAML Structure

## Play

```yaml id="d29"
- name:
```

Defines automation block.

---

## hosts

```yaml id="d30"
hosts: web
```

Target inventory group.

---

## become

```yaml id="d31"
become: yes
```

Run as root.

---

## tasks

```yaml id="d32"
tasks:
```

List of actions.

---

# Step 23: Run Playbook

```bash id="d33"
ansible-playbook -i inventory/hosts playbooks/apache.yml
```

---

# Step 24: Syntax Check

```bash id="d34"
ansible-playbook apache.yml --syntax-check
```

## Purpose

Checks:

* YAML formatting
* indentation
* syntax errors

---

# Step 25: Dry Run

```bash id="d35"
ansible-playbook apache.yml --check
```

## Description

Simulates changes without modifying system.

Called:

* check mode
* dry run

---

# PART 6 — Variables

Variables make playbooks reusable.

---

# Step 26: Create Variable

```yaml id="d36"
vars:
  pkg: httpd
```

---

# Step 27: Use Variable

```yaml id="d37"
name: "{{ pkg }}"
```

## Description

`{{ }}`
means:
Jinja2 variable substitution.

---

# PART 7 — Facts

Facts = system information.

---

# Step 28: Gather Facts

```bash id="d38"
ansible all -m setup
```

## Description

Collects:

* hostname
* OS
* memory
* IP
* CPU

---

# Step 29: Filter Facts

```bash id="d39"
ansible all -m setup -a "filter=ansible_distribution"
```

---

# PART 8 — Loops

Loops avoid repeating tasks.

---

# Step 30: Install Multiple Packages

```yaml id="d40"
- name: Install packages
  dnf:
    name: "{{ item }}"
    state: present
  loop:
    - httpd
    - vsftpd
    - mariadb
```

## Description

`item`
changes automatically:

* httpd
* vsftpd
* mariadb

---

# PART 9 — Conditions

---

# Step 31: Conditional Task

```yaml id="d41"
when: ansible_distribution == "RedHat"
```

## Description

Task executes only if condition true.

---

# PART 10 — Templates

Templates create dynamic files.

---

# Step 32: Create Template

```bash id="d42"
mkdir templates
vi templates/index.j2
```

Template:

```jinja2 id="d43"
Server Name: {{ ansible_hostname }}
```

---

# Step 33: Deploy Template

```yaml id="d44"
- template:
    src: index.j2
    dest: /var/www/html/index.html
```

---

# PART 11 — Handlers

Handlers restart services only when needed.

---

# Step 34: Define Handler

```yaml id="d45"
handlers:
  - name: restart apache
    service:
      name: httpd
      state: restarted
```

---

# Step 35: Notify Handler

```yaml id="d46"
notify: restart apache
```

---

# PART 12 — Roles

Roles organize automation.

---

# Step 36: Create Role

```bash id="d47"
ansible-galaxy init apache
```

---

# Step 37: Role Structure

```bash id="d48"
apache/
├── tasks/
├── handlers/
├── templates/
├── vars/
```

---

# Step 38: Add Role Task

```yaml id="d49"
# roles/apache/tasks/main.yml

- name: Install Apache
  dnf:
    name: httpd
    state: present
```

---

# Step 39: Use Role

```yaml id="d50"
roles:
  - apache
```

